---
Title: Inline functions
---

# Inline `func(…)`

The answer is func() { return 6*7 } today.

A function may return markdown, func() { return { inline: '*strong* and /italic/' } }, lexed inline.

Trailing prose is not part of it: func() { return 'one' } (see above), and a brace
inside a string does not end it: func() { return '}' } here.

Prose that merely mentions the func(x) notation stays prose.

A function that throws leaves a named error, func() { throw new Error('boom') }, and
the build carries on.
